\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The detection logic, with the count at each level. Three levels and no more: a \emph  {crossing} is an event requiring investigation, an \emph  {unattributed crossing} is a target for follow-up, and a \emph  {confirmed signal} -- recovered in a block of another observing session more than 1{} day away -- would be a detection. Coincidence with a catalogued transition is a flag and not a disposal, so all 56{} crossings continue past it; the spatial rank and the visibility fit are diagnostics attached to the middle level and decide nothing. The reserved hold-out is drawn as a separate branch because a transmitter in it would matter whatever its calibration role. Every count is read from the ledger, which lists every crossing the search produced, including those in the archival-tail blocks and the quality-failing block that no expectation is computed over, so the figure, the ledger and the text cannot disagree. The counts drawn are the primary crossings, one to a window; the 21{} secondary crossings of \S  \ref  {sec:technosearch} enter the same three levels and three{} reach the second, none the third.}}{7}{figure.4.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:chain}{{4}{7}{The detection logic, with the count at each level. Three levels and no more: a \emph {crossing} is an event requiring investigation, an \emph {unattributed crossing} is a target for follow-up, and a \emph {confirmed signal} -- recovered in a block of another observing session more than \EpSep {} day away -- would be a detection. Coincidence with a catalogued transition is a flag and not a disposal, so all \CnCross {} crossings continue past it; the spatial rank and the visibility fit are diagnostics attached to the middle level and decide nothing. The reserved hold-out is drawn as a separate branch because a transmitter in it would matter whatever its calibration role. Every count is read from the ledger, which lists every crossing the search produced, including those in the archival-tail blocks and the quality-failing block that no expectation is computed over, so the figure, the ledger and the text cannot disagree. The counts drawn are the primary crossings, one to a window; the \CkNSecondary {} secondary crossings of \S \ref {sec:technosearch} enter the same three levels and \CkNSecUnattrWord {} reach the second, none the third}{figure.4.4}{}}
