\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The survey ledger, part one: execution blocks and windows.} Each row carries its own number, and a group sums to the row whose number heads it. The primary census is the survey: unless a statement names one of the other sets, it is computed over that row; rows\nobreakspace  {}3.2 to 3.5 are the archival gap, and no result is formed on them. Hours are window-hours: on-source time summed over spectral windows, so the classes partition the hours as they partition the windows. The telescope on-source time behind the primary census is 281\,h, of which 153\,h carries at least one Class\nobreakspace  {}A window and 277\,h at least one Class\nobreakspace  {}B window -- figures that overlap and must not be added. Confirmed planet counts here and in the target list come from the NASA Exoplanet Archive{} \texttt  {pscomppars}{} table \citep  {NEA2013}, accessed 2026 October 4. Part two, Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:counts}, carries the events and the confirmation extents.}}{27}{table.A.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:blockledger}{{A1}{27}{\textbf {The survey ledger, part one: execution blocks and windows.} Each row carries its own number, and a group sums to the row whose number heads it. The primary census is the survey: unless a statement names one of the other sets, it is computed over that row; rows~3.2 to 3.5 are the archival gap, and no result is formed on them. Hours are window-hours: on-source time summed over spectral windows, so the classes partition the hours as they partition the windows. The telescope on-source time behind the primary census is \StTelHours \,h, of which \StTelHoursFine \,h carries at least one Class~A window and \StTelHoursCoarse \,h at least one Class~B window -- figures that overlap and must not be added. Confirmed planet counts here and in the target list come from the \SfHostCatalogue {} \SfHostTable {} table \citep {NEA2013}, accessed \SfHostDate . Part two, Table~\ref {tab:counts}, carries the events and the confirmation extents}{table.A.1}{}}
